From 750cd92002cad7fdee1c645235198a3366143040 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 00:41:11 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 30/38] venus: advertise only what the pinned protocol defines

The renderer's extension table and command dispatch are written against the
venus-protocol revision the renderer was developed on. This project pins one
protocol revision for the host and the guest together, because the guest Mesa
driver is sealed against the generated codecs, and that pin is older than the
renderer's own subproject.

Eight entries in the advertised extension table and one command dispatcher
name protocol entities the pinned revision does not define, so the renderer
does not compile against it. None of them is reachable: a guest sealed against
the same revision cannot encode a command or request an extension its own
generated codec does not know.

Drop those entries. Raising the pin is a guest-visible change and belongs to a
protocol epoch, not to a host build fix.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
